1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,410
That light was yours.

2
00:00:02,700 --> 00:00:04,550
One move later, it's mine.

3
00:00:05,060 --> 00:00:06,110
That's Borrowlight.

4
00:00:06,920 --> 00:00:10,550
A duel where every move leaves
your opponent a puzzle.

5
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:12,070
I'm Aryan.

6
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:15,070
Sharing VR can mean waiting for a turn,

7
00:00:15,320 --> 00:00:16,910
then learning a new set of controls.

8
00:00:17,580 --> 00:00:20,530
I wanted one headset to feel like
a shared game night.

9
00:00:20,960 --> 00:00:24,750
Quick turns, bare hands,
and a little friendly rivalry.

10
00:00:25,440 --> 00:00:27,990
The ribbon floats in front of you.

11
00:00:30,210 --> 00:00:31,590
Grab a knot. Lift it.

12
00:00:31,630 --> 00:00:32,460
Pull it closer.

13
00:00:32,910 --> 00:00:35,560
Bend the route through
those floating lights,

14
00:00:35,750 --> 00:00:36,520
then let go.

15
00:00:37,110 --> 00:00:39,180
The pulse fires on release.

16
00:00:39,490 --> 00:00:41,300
You see the route before you commit.

17
00:00:42,390 --> 00:00:43,680
Claim a fresh light.

18
00:00:43,930 --> 00:00:44,660
One point.

19
00:00:44,930 --> 00:00:47,200
Cross a light your rival claimed.

20
00:00:47,790 --> 00:00:49,300
Two points for the steal.

21
00:00:49,550 --> 00:00:50,900
It then burns out,

22
00:00:51,110 --> 00:00:52,770
so you can't farm it forever.

23
00:00:52,810 --> 00:00:56,580
The knot you just moved
locks for the next turn.

24
00:00:57,390 --> 00:00:58,060
Now it's your turn.

25
00:00:59,390 --> 00:01:02,240
You get the ribbon I just left behind.

26
00:01:04,630 --> 00:01:06,640
That lovely route I used to score?

27
00:01:06,970 --> 00:01:08,200
It might be your shortcut.

28
00:01:08,550 --> 00:01:10,540
So I have to think one move ahead:

29
00:01:10,810 --> 00:01:13,080
can I score without setting you up?

30
00:01:14,710 --> 00:01:16,920
Left and right are separate player roles.

31
00:01:18,190 --> 00:01:19,880
Only the active hand can play.

32
00:01:20,010 --> 00:01:21,530
You can also pass the headset,

33
00:01:21,570 --> 00:01:24,160
with a ready screen between players.

34
00:01:24,350 --> 00:01:27,040
Here, I'm demonstrating both roles myself.

35
00:01:27,650 --> 00:01:28,280
Playing alone?

36
00:01:28,690 --> 00:01:30,680
Challenge the bot.

37
00:01:31,230 --> 00:01:32,680
Same field. Same rules.

38
00:01:32,810 --> 00:01:34,380
And yes, it can steal back.

39
00:01:34,890 --> 00:01:38,140
Two six-move heists swap who starts.

40
00:01:38,490 --> 00:01:39,520
Highest total wins.

41
00:01:40,450 --> 00:01:42,180
Need a change of pace?

42
00:01:42,690 --> 00:01:43,960
There's the rest of the arcade.

43
00:01:44,510 --> 00:01:47,190
Steer, rotate and drop blocks
in Aftershape.

44
00:01:47,230 --> 00:01:49,970
Touch your next move in Tic-tac-toe.

45
00:01:50,010 --> 00:01:52,580
Or settle it with Rock Paper Scissors,

46
00:01:53,210 --> 00:01:56,300
and replay the clash in slow motion.

47
00:01:57,670 --> 00:02:01,060
I built this in Unity
for standalone Quest 2.

48
00:02:01,510 --> 00:02:03,340
Testing taught me something important:

49
00:02:03,590 --> 00:02:06,630
tiny buttons and extra confirmations
break the flow.

50
00:02:06,670 --> 00:02:08,550
So I enlarged touch targets,

51
00:02:08,590 --> 00:02:11,800
and made releasing the knot
the move itself.

52
00:02:12,710 --> 00:02:13,820
While doing the coding,

53
00:02:14,010 --> 00:02:16,400
I made sure it also runs on Quest 3.

54
00:02:18,010 --> 00:02:20,880
Next: more players testing the duels,

55
00:02:21,050 --> 00:02:22,900
deeper bot strategy,

56
00:02:23,390 --> 00:02:25,440
and polish across headsets.

57
00:02:26,210 --> 00:02:27,620
The mission stays simple.

58
00:02:27,830 --> 00:02:30,780
Turn one Quest into a shared game night.

59
00:02:30,910 --> 00:02:31,860
Your hands. Your move.

60
00:02:34,440 --> 00:02:35,190
Thank you.
